  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Satya Rani And Another vs State Of Haryana on 6 May, 2024 Author: Mahabir Singh Sindhu Bench: Mahabir Singh Sindhu Neutral Citation No:=2024:PHHC:062709 Crm-M M No.19246 of 2024 (O&M) 105 In The High Court Of Punjab And Haryana At Chandigarh Crm-M M No. No.19246 of 2024 (O&M) Date of Decision: 06.05.2024 Satya Rani and another ......... Petitioners Versus State of Haryana ......... Respondent Coram: Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Mahabir Singh Sindhu Present:- Mr. Birender Singh Rana, Senior Advocate assisted by Mr. Karanbir Singh Kahlon, Kahlon, Advocate for the petitioner petitioners . M Kiran Pal Singh, Aag, Haryana for the respondent. Mr. **** Mahabir Singh Sindhu, J. Satya Rani And Another vs State Of Haryana on 6 May, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/52775079/ 1 (2) This Court, on 29.04.2024, passed the following order: order:- \"Present second petition under Section 438 of Cr.P.C. for grant of pre-arrest arrest bail in FIR No. 428 dated 18.11.2023 under Section 406, 420, 120B IPC (later on added Section 409 IPC), registered at Police Station Butana, District Karnal.",
    "facts": "Second petition has been filed under Section 438 of the Code of Criminal Procedure, Procedure 1973 for grant of pre-arrest arrest bail to the petitioner petitioners in FIR No.428 dated 18.11.2023, 18.11.2023 under Sections 406, 420, 120 120-B of the Indian Penal Code, 1860 (Section 409 IPC added later on) on), registered at Police Station Butana,, District Karnal. Be shown in the Urgent list. Satya Rani And Another vs State Of Haryana on 6 May, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/52775079/ 2 (3) It is alleged that all three accused have neither delivered 15196.7455 quintals of ri rice ce to the Food Corporation of India; nor the amount was deposited by them. The physical inspection of the Mill Mill was conducted by the department on 14.10.2023 and no paddy/rice was found in the premises.",
    "arguments": "Learned Senior Counsel contends that in similar FIR(s), IR(s), accused were granted the concession of pre-arrest pre arrest bail by learned Sessions Court; but the petitioners have been denied the benefit without any cogent reasons. Also contends that although pre-arrest arrest bail of the petitioners was declined by this Court on 08.01.2024; but in view of the above factual position, petitioners be granted the concession on the ground of parity. (7) Per contra, contra learned earned State Counsel on instructions while opposing the prayer submits that on earlier occasion, pre pre-arrest arrest bail of both the 3 of 5 Neutral Citation No:=2024:PHHC:062709 CRM-M petitioners was as rejected by this Court on 08.01.2024 while passing a reasoned order and the same has not been [LEAKAGE_MASK] till date date;; hence, second petition is not maintainable without any changed circumstances."
  },
